- meat
---

= Filling Mixture =

Slice the @asparagus{1%bunch}(approx. 10 young stalks, trimmed) into lengths of about 5 cm. Half-fill a #large non-stick frying pan{} with water and bring to the boil. Add the asparagus, bring back to the boil, and cook for ~{1%minute} until just tender. Drain and rinse under running water until cold, then pat dry.

Trim any fat off the bacon and cut into 1 cm strips. Return the frying pan to a low heat, add the @olive oil{1%tsp}. Gently fry the @onion{1%medium}(finely sliced) and @back bacon {5%rashers}(dry-cured, smoked) until lightly browned, stirring regularly.

Add the onion and bacon to the bowl with the asparagus, toss lightly, and leave to cool.

Preheat oven to 180°C. Place a #baking tray{} in the oven to heat.

= Pastry Case =

Lightly oil a #loose-based fluted flan tin, 20cm diameter, 3.5cm deep{}.

Place a sheet of @filo pastry{4%sheets} in the flan tin, pressing it firmly against the base and sides, and brush with a little @olive oil{1%tbsp}. Repeat with three more sheets, rotating each by 45°. Roll and crumple the overhanging pastry back onto the rim of the tin, lifting slightly above it, and brush lightly with the remaining oil.

= White Sauce =

Put the @cornflour{25%g} in a #non-stick saucepan{} and stir in 50 ml of the @milk{300%ml} to make a thin paste. Add a further 200ml of the milk and stir well. Bring to a simmer, stirring constantly.

Cook for ~{1%minute} over a medium heat, stirring, until the sauce is thick and smooth.

Season with @sea salt{}(flaked) and @black pepper{}(freshly ground), then remove from the heat, and stir in the rest of the milk to cool and loosen the sauce.

Stir in the @eggs{3}(beaten) until thoroughly combined.

= Assemble Flan =

Scatter half the asparagus, bacon, and onion mixture over the base of the pastry case. Pour the white sauce gently on top. Scatter the remaining asparagus and bacon mixture on top and press down lightly. Sprinkle evenly with the @cheddar, extra-mature{25%g}(finely grated).

Bake on the preheated baking tray in the centre of the oven for 25 to ~{30%minutes}, until the pastry is lightly browned and crisp and the filling is set.

Take the flan out of the oven and leave to cool in the tin for ~{10%minutes} before removing. Serve warm or cold.